# Live like the main route: searching every catalog, the recent searches,
# and connecting a catalog of your own.
tap Back
wait-for Catalogs
tap Project Gutenberg
wait-for Popular
tap-id search
wait-for Search every catalog
expect Only this catalog
tap-id search-all
wait-for Every catalog in the list
tap-id query
wait-for-id kb.enter
type austen
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for every catalog
# Every catalog answers in its own time over the live network.
wait-idle 30000
wait-for Jane Austen
clean
shot gutenbird-search-every
# The search is remembered as a recent search on the search screen.
tap-id search
wait-for Recent searches
expect austen
expect Every catalog in the list
clean
shot gutenbird-search-recent
tap Back
wait-for every catalog
# A catalog of your own: an empty address is refused with the reason, an
# address is typed on the keyboard, and a server that does not answer says so.
tap-id catalogs
wait-for Catalogs
tap-id add-catalog
wait-for Connect catalog
tap Check connection
wait-for HTTPS address
clean
shot gutenbird-add-empty
tap Add server address
wait-for-id kb.enter
type https://opds.invalid
tap-id kb.enter
wait-for https://opds.invalid
scenario host-down
tap Check connection
wait-for did not answer
clean
shot gutenbird-add-host-down
scenario normal
tap Back
wait-for Catalogs
expect-missing opds.invalid
# A recent search should run the way the switch beside it says: across
# every catalog when that is on.
tap Project Gutenberg
wait-for Popular
tap-id search
wait-for Recent searches
expect Every catalog in the list
tap-id recent-0
wait-for every catalog
wait-idle 30000
wait-for Jane Austen
expect every catalog
